    pr_ref:  # 0d1b
    description: "PROBLEM. A framework rule keyed on a base class (`base_class:` on a class, `parent_base_class:` + `method_name:` on a method; framework_patterns.Pattern) matches the DECLARED bases only: `symbol.meta[\"base_classes\"]` / `meta[\"parent_base_classes\"]` as the analyzer wrote them. There is no hierarchy walk in framework_patterns.py (grep transitiv|hierarch|ancestor|mro: nothing). A class that extends an in-repo subclass of the framework base is invisible to the rule.\n\nINSTANCE (mlflow, found measuring WI-sorop's python half, 2026-11-03): mlflow/server/graphql/graphql_schema_extensions.py has `class Query(QueryType)` and `class Mutation(MutationType)` with `QueryType(graphene.ObjectType)` / `MutationType(graphene.ObjectType)` in autogenerated_graphql_schema.py. Their resolve_* methods (resolve_test on Query, and the extension classes' resolve_experiment / resolve_model_versions / resolve_value) are real Graphene resolvers; the WI-sorop rule `method_name ^resolve_\\w+$ + parent_base_class ^(graphene\\.)?ObjectType$` reaches the 7 direct subclasses in autogenerated_graphql_schema.py and none of these. Pre-registered as \"must not gain\" under the shipped rule, and they did not; the miss is this item.\n\nFAMILY. Every base-class-keyed rule in every YAML, every language: flask-restful Resource subclass of a project ApiResource(Resource); Django View subclass chains; java HttpServlet via a project BaseServlet (WI-losij's servlet rule will have the same hole); objc. Not measured beyond mlflow.\n\nFIX CANDIDATES. (a) framework_patterns resolves a class's transitive in-repo bases through the class symbols of the same analysis (the inheritance linker's `_transitive_bases` BFS already exists for linkers, WI-jusih) and matches the rule against the closure, recording `matched_base_class` as the declared base that led there; a method inherits its class's closure for parent_base_class. (b) the analyzers stamp a `base_classes_transitive` list at pass 1.5. (a) keeps the producers unchanged and is one consumer. Measure: mlflow (4 resolvers), one flask-restful or Django app with an intermediate base, cert-manager/caddy for a non-python control (no change expected).\n\nNOT ASSERTED: that the external part of a hierarchy (framework base -> framework intermediate -> project class) can be resolved; only in-repo intermediates are in scope."  # 0d1b
    fields: {}  # 0d1b
